  "body": "#698: the light theme's viewport stayed dark, because the 3D pass cleared to a fixed colour. It now follows the theme, and everything drawn over the viewport reads on a light ground. The light values were tuned on screen with the reporter in a running build. The dark theme looks as before; every dark ink is asserted equal to its old value.\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **Viewport ground:** a theme token, `Tokens::viewport`. Light is `#DDE1E7`; dark keeps the old clear colour. Theme files can set it with a new `viewport` key. The 3D pass clears to the live theme's ground.\r\n- **Light-ground inks**, new module `ground_ink.rs`:\r\n  - Toolpath moves: deep feed green, plus the rapid blue and plunge red the reporter picked. All three clear 3:1 on the ground.\r\n  - Saturated boundary roles.\r\n  - Wireframe edge (a new shader uniform), world axes, and the region, retract, cut, pick and hover overlays.\r\n  - The corner control hint and the playback tool marker, which were white.\r\n- **Colour-vision modes** (added after review): protan/deutan and tritan get light-ground sets too (`RED_GREEN_LIGHT_GROUND`, `TRITAN_LIGHT_GROUND`), changing only the line inks. On the light ground their dark-tuned lines read 1.01-2.8:1 (a pale yellow feed and a white \"open\" boundary). Each light set keeps its eye's surviving axis (blue-yellow, or red-cyan) and moves the pale end to near-black, so lightness still carries the pairs. Every must-distinguish pair passes the CIEDE2000 floor (weakest: protan 25.7, deutan 27.7, tritan 24.4), and every line ink clears 3:1 (3.5-14.6:1).\r\n- **Dimmed paths:** unselected paths under \"Show all toolpaths\" fade toward a light ground instead of being scaled toward black. At 0.45 that turned every hue into near-black, and the lines couldn't be told apart.\r\n- **View cube:** in light theme, the faces are mid grey, a step under the ground, with darker edges and dark labels. The four buttons under it match.\r\n  - The Axes button's triad is now centred and symmetric (equal arms, 120° apart), in saturated X/Y/Z colours, in both themes. Before, it was off-centre and pastel.\r\n- **Hover (light only):** `field_hover` and egui's hover fill are the viewport grey, with dark ink. This covers the toolbar, menus, the tree and buttons. Dark keeps its steel-blue hover.\r\n- **Window title bars (light only):** egui's `open.weak_bg_fill` is the window fill and `open.fg_stroke` the text. They were egui's dark defaults, so light windows had black title bars with invisible icons. Dark keeps egui's own values (pinned).\r\n- **Debug info window:** draws its own title row (new `window_chrome.rs`). Its collapse arrow hovers grey, and close hovers red with a white X, like the OS caption buttons. egui's built-in title bar paints these glyphs with no hover fill. **Why it is in this PR:** the reporter hit it during the light-theme check. On the light ground the window's arrow and close glyphs were invisible, then vanished on hover. It is a light-theme readability fix of the same kind as the rest.\r\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/698-light-viewport.md`.\r\n\r\n## How it was tested\r\n\r\nNew pinning tests:\r\n- `egui_app::viewport_ground_tests`:\r\n  - `the_light_viewport_is_light_and_the_dark_one_stays_dark`\r\n  - `every_overlay_ink_clears_3_to_1_on_the_light_viewport`\r\n  - `the_light_palette_move_inks_clear_3_to_1`\r\n  - `the_light_palette_is_the_hand_tuned_set`\r\n  - `a_dimmed_path_fades_toward_a_light_ground_and_darkens_on_a_dark_one`\r\n  - `the_light_wireframe_and_axis_inks_clear_3_to_1`\r\n  - `the_light_cube_sits_a_step_under_the_viewport_with_darker_edges`\r\n  - `the_dark_cube_keeps_its_greys`\r\n  - `light_hover_is_the_viewport_grey_with_dark_ink_and_dark_keeps_its_accent`\r\n  - `the_dark_ground_keeps_the_house_inks`\r\n  - `every_mode_wears_its_light_set_on_a_light_ground`\r\n  - `the_light_colour_vision_sets_pass_the_cvd_gate_and_clear_3_to_1`\r\n  - `the_dark_title_bar_keeps_eguis_own_open_fill`\r\n- `egui_app::debug_info_tests::the_title_row_folds_the_window_and_its_close_button_closes_it`: folds, unfolds and closes through the AccessKit labels.\r\n\r\nGates:\r\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick`) on 6177922d: green. ui lib 468 passed, plus the boundary, boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, gpu_render, operations and theme_files suites; 0 failed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- No snapshot PNG touched.\r\n\r\nVisual check: the reporter tuned the light colours over several rounds in a running Windows build, and approved them.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The light pixel snapshot golden (`egui_app_light`) will differ on the viewport, hover and title bars. Per the pixel-snapshot law it is regenerated at the cut, not here.\r\n- The light colour-vision sets were checked by the simulation gate (Machado 2009 with CIEDE2000, the same as the dark sets), not by a colour-vision-deficient viewer.\r\n- The light-set literals live in `ground_ink.rs`, not in theme tokens, so a theme file cannot change them yet (review note 4: a follow-up).\r\n- Part shading and the selected-part amber on the light ground were not re-tuned.\r\n- Boundary role inks on the light ground are under 3:1 (hue chosen over contrast). They are pinned as chosen, and listed as open in the decision note.\r\n- The other four floating windows keep egui's title bar. It is now themed, but has no caption hover fill.\r\n- macOS and Linux were not run.\r\n\r\n`theme.rs` is at 402 lines.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The light theme now has a light viewport, with toolpath, overlay, view cube, hover and window title bar colours that read on it (#698)\r\n\r\nEffort: low (the issue's label). The work grew past it: 4 more files than planned and a new window title row. Not escalated, because the work was steered visually with the reporter in the main session.\r\n\r\nFixes #698\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
